meta {
  name: Share with everyone
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

patch {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/books/{{bookId}}/scope
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {
    "shared": true
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.scope: eq canon
}

docs {
  Moves the book from `personal` to `canon` — readable by every signed-in user, and the
  only pool an assessment can draw from.

  The body carries a boolean, not a scope. The client says "share this"; the server
  decides which enum value that means. A body that named the scope directly would be one
  refactor away from accepting a value nobody intended, and this is the column the whole
  privacy model rests on.

  Audited in both directions. This is the only action in the product that changes *who
  can read something*.
}
